            <ArticleTitle>Progressive development of a left ventricular thrombus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a patient with ischemic heart disease and terminal left ventricular failure, echocardiographic techniques (single-crystal M-mode echocardiograms and bidimensional, linear, dynamically focussed multiscan recordings) allowed the detection and follow-up of a left ventricular thrombus, later documented at autopsy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
